## 3. Recurring job — triage inbound {{ email_address }} mail

Before invoking triage, run the waiting-draft inventory once synchronously:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m cs review --json
```

Together with step 2c's actual tasks result, this retains the current run's
symbolic workset inputs. Proceed to the canonical unanswered discovery even if
native output was clipped or persisted; do not first page the raw review.
Discovery creates the source-bound v2 view containing all recurring material.
Complete every automatic material/envelope part, or the literal page plans,
before effects or an exhaustive review report. Reuse these same retained inputs
in triage and step 4c; do not issue duplicate full reads. Missing/incomplete
inputs remain UNKNOWN. A global assignment warning does not hold every root;
keep each named exact-root hold and all fresh selected-root checks mandatory.
Scheduled discovery emits `triage_workset`: at most two exact conversation
revisions across inbound, task-only work and draft replacements share one
reservation. Deep reads and composition outside it are refused by the CLI.
Start no evidence subagents and no waiting/poll loops. Preserve full inventories,
named held work and every deferred root in the final report; reservation and
deferral do not mean answered, handled or closed. Continue all recurring phases.

Invoke the `cs-triage-mail` sub-skill using the host's native skill mechanism.

It finds inbound {{ email_address }} mail needing a human answer, reads full bodies
(not snippets) via the engine and composes drafts **through the engine**
(memory + trained voice + exact threading). It leaves engine drafts for the
operator and **sends nothing**, even if the effective mode says `send`; it
escalates judgment calls / out-of-scope / angry mail rather than
auto-answering. It checks existing exact-thread drafts without treating a
draft as handled or closing an assignment. Capture what it reports (drafted / escalated / nothing to
do). If it has nothing to do, that is a valid outcome — record it and move
on.

Keep the sub-skill's `human_work`, ordinary `escalated` owner/age, closed audit
and reopened-thread decisions in the consolidated report. A positive reply
candidate with an unreadable peer remains UNKNOWN; do not summarize it as
answered or remove it because a local handled record exists. A nonautomatic
member reply needs human verification and explicit assignment.

